  "notes": [
    "All 29 official USPTO image-ppubs grant PDFs were re-downloaded on 2026-11-17 after the /workspace snapshot restore around 12:51–12:52 Asia/Taipei. Each officialSHA256 and pdfByteLength was computed from the official PDF bytes actually kept in out/batch-1/pdfs/.",
    "For every record, the official image-ppubs SHA-256 differs from the bibliography fingerprint of the Google-hosted USPTO grant PDF. The Google-hosted copy was also downloaded, matched the bibliography hash, and was used only as a locator or cross-check, not as the Claim 1 source.",
    "Every Claim 1 verbatim string was transcribed from the official page image (the claims-start page, and the next page only when Claim 1 continued). Full-document OCR was not used. Line-end hyphenation was joined. Printed typographical errors were kept as printed.",
    "titleMatch compares the official page-1 printed title with the batch originalTitle. Case-only differences were treated as a match. The only titleMatch false is US8659933B2 (HERETO vs HETERO), as listed under bibliographicMismatches.",
    "assigneeMatch is true for all 29. Official assignee lines often add a city and jurisdiction after the company name in the batch record. US8258020B2 prints “Crossbar Inc.” (no comma) on the official front page; US8619459B1 prints “Crossbar, Inc.” Official location typography such as Santa Clara, San Jose, Kitakyushu-shi, or Hsinchu County was noted in the individual reviews and was not treated as an assignee mismatch.",
    "Certificates of Correction appear in the official PDFs for US8513636B2 (page 13; January 12, 2016; related-application filing date in the specification only), US8619459B1 (page 24; December 22, 2015; specification provisional number/date only), US8659933B2 (page 26; title and specification only, as above), and US6956258B2 (pages 27–28; September 26, 2006; item (56) references only). None of those certificates amends Claim 1.",
    "Selected Claim 1 typography kept as printed includes: US8723154B2 “a switching media.”; US8750019B2 “are rovided below” and a missing article before “polycrystalline silicon-germanium material layer”; USRE46335E1 reissue brackets and italics, including “; [and]” and “the read voltage[.];”; US7269047B1 “reducing number of times” and “stored as a digital data”; US7623368B2 “p-type body” then “P-type body,” and “formed atop of a substrate”; US7248507B2 “threshold voltaae” and “lingering ehanae”; US11736285B2 “an one-time programmable (OTP) device” and “the another comparison result.” Dependent-claim typography such as US8659003B2 Claim 2 “the first call” and US7623368B2 Claim 2 “said the MOS” was noted only as a boundary observation.",
    "US9230813B2 FIGS. 1–3 are labeled prior art and were not used as the primary figure alignment. Other prior-art figures (including US8088688B1 FIGS. 1–5, US8258020B2 FIG. 1, US8659003B2 FIG. 2, and US7248507B2 FIGS. 14–18) were likewise not used as primary alignment.",
    "Each review was written to /workspace/nvm-claim1/out/batch-1/{publicationNumber}.json and appended as one compact JSON line to reviews.jsonl. The 29 JSON files and the 29 jsonl lines are identical for each publication number. There are no remaining or unresolvable records in batch 1."
